      // Project: iViDo - Document Management
      pIvidoCat: "Document Management · Resilient Architecture · High-Concurrency",
      pIvidoName: "iViDo · Document Management & Hybrid Contingency",
      pIvidoPitch: "High-concurrency corporate document service built on Node.js (Express 5 + ESM) and multi-worker cluster, engineered for progressive migration and total contingency against the legacy MyDoc system (PHP/IIS/MSSQL). Features on-the-fly dynamic PDF stamping and barcode generation, shared disk caching, and real-time metadata resolution with the corporate ERP.",
      pIvidoKpi1Num: "100% Uptime",
      pIvidoKpi1Lbl: "Active contingency against legacy server downtime",
      pIvidoKpi2Num: "< 150 ms",
      pIvidoKpi2Lbl: "Cached PDF delivery vs 3-5 s in legacy SOAP",
      pIvidoKpi3Num: "+15,000 /mo",
      pIvidoKpi3Lbl: "Documents processed with stamping and audit logging",
      pIvidoBullet1: "<strong>Master/Cluster Multi-Worker Architecture (cluster.mjs):</strong> Centralized HTTP Master with Active Directory NTLM authentication and <code>X-API-Key</code> bypass. Intelligent routing: 1 isolated SOAP Worker (preventing concurrent ticket collisions with legacy system) and N Cache Workers in Round-Robin for read operations, APIs, and UI.",
      pIvidoBullet2: "<strong>On-the-Fly Stamping & PDF Manipulation (pdf-lib & bwip-js):</strong> Dynamic document injection of status seals (<code>EST_XX.pdf</code>), Code 128 barcodes, forecast dates, comments, and forensic audit footer (requesting AD user, workstation, and timestamp).",
      pIvidoBullet3: "<strong>AS/400 ERP Connector & Unattended EDM Ingestion (conectorEdm.mjs):</strong> Persistent UTF-8 (<code>CCSID=1208</code>) ODBC client with auto-reconnect and serialized mutex. Resolves purchase orders, suppliers, and raw materials in real time following scan of material delivery notes.",
